text.section:
To administer the scholarship program, the Board shall promulgate regulations which shall include, but are not limited to:

Qualifications of applicants;


Criteria for award of the scholarship to assure that a recipient will fulfill the practice obligations established in this section;


Standards to assure that these scholarships increase access to dental hygiene care for individuals who are indigent or who are recipients of public assistance;


Assurances that residents of Virginia, as determined by § 23.1-502, students of economically disadvantaged backgrounds and residents of medically underserved areas are given preference in determining scholarship eligibility and awards;


Assurances that a scholarship recipient will practice as a dental hygienist in an underserved area of the Commonwealth within two years following completion of training;


Methods for reimbursement to the Commonwealth by a recipient who fails to complete the educational program or who fails to honor the obligation to engage in practice as a dental hygienist for a period of years equal to the number of annual scholarships received;


Procedures for reimbursing any recipient who has repaid the Commonwealth for part or all of any scholarship and who later fulfills the terms of his contract; and


Methods for reporting data related to the recipients of the scholarships.
